course: dictionary
lesson: 92
title: Words that change to fit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adaptable means able to change to suit new situations or places. Think of a tool that can be used for many jobs, or a person who can change when life changes.
explain: «Red foxes are clever and adaptable» tells us that foxes can live in many places and still do well. They eat mice, rabbits, worms, insects, fruit and scraps, so they are not fussy about their food.
explain: People can be adaptable too. A child who settles in quickly after moving to a new school is adaptable. The word praises someone who copes well with change.
fact: Adaptable means able to change to suit new situations or places.
fact: An adaptable thing can be changed for different uses.
fact: Useful phrases are «highly adaptable» and «adaptable to», as in «adaptable to new places».
fact: Foxes eat mice, rabbits, worms, insects, fruit and scraps.
fact: In many stories foxes are sly tricksters, but real foxes are clever and adaptable, eat almost anything and learn quickly.
exercise: «Red foxes are clever and adaptable.» What does adaptable mean here? | Always sleeping in the same den | *Able to change to suit new places | Only found in one country | Very slow to learn
exercise: Foxes eat mice, rabbits, worms, insects, fruit and scraps. What does this list show about foxes? | They never leave the woods | *They can eat many kinds of food, so they can adapt | They eat only fruit | They only eat meat
exercise: «The new girl was adaptable and made friends fast.» Find and copy the word that means able to change to suit new situations. | *adaptable | friends | new | girl
test: A pupil who settles quickly into a new school is described as | lazy | *adaptable | noisy | tired
test: An adaptable tool can | never change its shape | *be used for different jobs | be used only once | only work in one place
exam: Which best describes adaptable? | Sad and tired | *Able to change to suit new situations | Very loud and noisy | Always exactly the same
